WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.053
Next we have NOT NOT is used when we want to exclude

00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:10.003
a condition In this example we keep active patients
but we exclude

00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:16.189
two diagnoses Notice the parentheses around the
diagnosis condition They

00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:19.230
make it very clear which part of the logic we are
reversing

00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:25.049
The query is available in the SQL box Run it here in

00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:29.559
the browser first Look at the results and confirm
that the excluded

00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:35.226
diagnoses do not appear You can also copy the query
into pgAdmin

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:39.493
and run it against the same practice tables One
important point is

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:43.951
that NOT does not magically solve missing values If
a condition is

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:48.346
UNKNOWN because of null applying NOT still leaves it
UNKNOWN We will

00:00:48.371 --> 00:00:50.407
see why that matters in a few slides
